From 5f19e7057e640fcc5a92969df82c0f12f2991aa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:54:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hamoa, glymur: Disable the crypto engine

Since 7.3 the QCE driver is BROKEN (df373d39c6f0, "crypto: qce - Mark
QCE as BROKEN"), so nothing binds to the crypto node. fw_devlink still
counts it as a consumer of the interconnects it names, so on the X1
aggre2_noc and mc_virt never reach sync_state(). mc_virt then keeps its
boot-time vote on DDR, and in suspend the SoC never collapses CX or puts
DDR in self-refresh.

Disable the node on the X1 (hamoa) and the X2 (glymur), whose crypto
engine names aggre1_noc and mc_virt the same way.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>

[virtudude: only the glymur hunk; the hamoa hunk does not apply to this tree]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
index 65a398c0a992..52f04a1ff554 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
@@ -4126,6 +4126,8 @@ crypto: crypto@1dfa000 {
 			interconnects = <&aggre1_noc MASTER_CRYPTO QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
 					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
 			interconnect-names = "memory";
+
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
 		tcsr_mutex: hwlock@1f40000 {
